  "notes": "Zipped copy of the 4TU release also held loose as dataset_22. The zip stores the Cell91 CSV twice (identical CRC); it is counted once. Cell spec from LG's official INR18650 MJ1 3500mAh product specification. The author README claims cell-level temperature measurements, but every locally available measurement CSV header was checked and contains no temperature channel (17 loose CSVs in dataset_22, 18 archive CSVs in dataset_23). Local cell-temperature data are absent at this inspected source scope. The extracted cycle total is a count of current-sign discharge events because no cycle-index column is delivered; dynamic drive reversals may create many events within one aging cycle. It must not be used as a verified count of physical aging cycles."
=======
  "notes": "Zipped copy of the 4TU release also held loose as dataset_22. The zip stores the Cell91 CSV twice (identical CRC); it is counted once. Cell spec from LG's official INR18650 MJ1 3500mAh product specification. The author README claims cell-level temperature measurements, but every locally available measurement CSV header was checked and contains no temperature channel (17 loose CSVs in dataset_22, 18 archive CSVs in dataset_23). Local cell-temperature data are absent at this inspected source scope. The extracted cycle total is a count of current-sign discharge events because no cycle-index column is delivered; dynamic drive reversals may create many events within one aging cycle. It must not be used as a verified count of physical aging cycles. Charging profile: same 17 cells as dataset_22. D2.3 (read in full) also lists the planned lifecycle matrix: charge CC-CV at 0.5C with discharge 0.5C or 3C (Table 2), and discharge 1.5C with charge CC-CV 0.5C or 1C (Table 3), at 0, 10, 25 and 45 C within a 10-90% SOC window updated after each check-up; the delivered files cover 25 and 45 C and the pairs (charge, discharge) 0.5/0.5, 0.5/1.5 and 1.0/1.5 C, and the 3C pairs (and the 0 and 10 C cells run at TUV) are not in this release."
